===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|head=[[pull]]-[[down]]}}

# {{lb|en|computing}} A dynamic [[menu]]; a list of [[option]]s in a computer application which appears below a heading when it is selected, and remains only as long as the [[user]] needs it.
#: {{cot|en|dropdown|drop-down}}
# {{lb|en|biology}} A [[technique]] by which a [[protein]] is [[brought]] [[down]] in a [[test]] [[tube]] by [[another]].
# {{lb|en|signal processing}} The [[conversion]] of [[video]] [[footage]] to a higher [[frame rate]] by [[duplicate|duplicating]] certain [[frame]]s.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=David Mellor|title=Sound Person's Guide to Video|page=216
|passage=When a TV monitor is in shot, and the film is transferred to video through the normal 2:3 '''pulldown''' there will be a strobing effect where the film and video frame rates clash.}}
# {{lb|en|usually|uncountable}}{{c|en|Morning glory family plants}} [[dodder|Dodder]] (plant of genus ''Cuscuta'').
# {{lb|en|juggling}} A trick done with [[ring]]s where each ring is pulled down over the head instead of being caught and held in the hand.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1994|title=KNOW THE GAME - JUGGLING|author=Haggis McLeod|passage=Another classic trick with rings is the ''''pull-down''''. This can only be done with rings that fit easily over your head.|ISBN=0-7136-3817-6}}
#* '''2004''', Luke Holman, [http://groups.google.com/group/rec.juggling/browse_thread/thread/a6cf29c2f2597e96/db89d143ac6eb589?hl=en&ie=UTF-8&q=%22+ring+pulldown%22#db89d143ac6eb589 Hardest, most tech trick on the net], May 12 2004 via Google Groups
#*: For example, the 11 ring '''pulldown''' didn't stick in my head because I don't really juggle rings, and I have no conception of how hard it is.
# {{lb|en|exercise}} An [[exercise]] mostly performed by pulling [[cable]]s, a [[bar]], or [[handle]]s from a machine situated diagonally to the front top of the sportsman and targetting the [[rear]] [[muscle]]s.

